  <title>Adjust inventory</title>

  <p>Click <gui>Adjust inventory</gui> on a product's <link
  xref="product_edit_main#inventory">Inventory</link> tab to correct its stock
  at one location, outside a full count.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Check the <gui>Product</gui> and choose the
    <gui>Location</gui>. <gui>Current inventory</gui> shows how many the books
    have there; <gui>History</gui> opens <link
    xref="inventory_history"/>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Under <gui>Adjust inventory</gui>, type how many to add, or a
    negative number to take away. <gui>Adjusted inventory</gui> shows the
    result.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Adjustment reason</gui>, such as Broken, Lost, or
    Lost and found.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Apply</gui>.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>The value of the stock added or taken away is posted between the
  product's inventory account and an expense account, so the product needs an
  inventory account; a message says so if it has none.</p>

</page>
